==English==

===Etymology 1===
From ''to [[spill]]'', ''[[the]]'' and ''[[bean]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/spɪl ðə biːnz/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[spill]] [[the]] [[beans]]|spills the beans|spilling the beans|spilled the beans}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To [[reveal]] a [[secret]]; to [[disclose]].
#: ''They had planned it as a surprise party, but somebody '''spilled the beans'''.''

====Syonyms====

*To disclose
*To give away

===Etymology 2===
From the fact that [[beans]] cause [[flatulence]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/spɪl ðə biːnz/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[spill]] [[the]] [[beans]]|spills the beans|spilling the beans|spilled the beans}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To [[fart]].
#: ''Someone suddenly '''spilled the beans''' during the meeting.''

====Synonyms====
* to [[squeak]]
* to [[break wind]], to [[fart]], to [[trump]], to [[beef]], to make a stinker.

